  "reasoning": "Cook\u2019s statewide Partisan Voting Index rates Iowa at R+6, indicating a structural Republican edge in federal races.[1][4] However, recent cycle data show multiple signs of competitiveness: Cook shifted the 2026 U.S. Senate race rating from \u201clikely Republican\u201d to \u201cleans Republican,\u201d and analysts describe Iowa races as \u201csurprisingly competitive\u201d for Democrats, suggesting a more balanced environment than the underlying PVI.[3][12] In the key IA-1 House race, July 2026 polling from The Bullfinch Group shows Democrat Christina Bohannan leading Republican Mariannette Miller-Meeks by 5 points (40% to 35%), providing a current-cycle Democratic edge in at least one major federal contest despite the state\u2019s GOP registration advantage of roughly 10 percentage points.[2][6][8]",
